    "description": "Coastal GasLink Pipeline Project is a 670-kilometre natural gas transmission project connecting northeastern British Columbia to LNG Canada’s export terminal in Kitimat. Its customers or end markets include LNG Canada and upstream natural gas production in the Montney region. The operating model is an asset-heavy transmission pipeline supported by long-term transportation arrangements rather than merchant commodity exposure. Operations are concentrated in British Columbia along the Dawson Creek-to-Kitimat corridor. Public materials indicate route length of 670 kilometres and design capacity of approximately 2.1 Bcf/d. Current ownership includes TC Energy, which retained 35% when KKR and AIMCo acquired a combined 65% interest in 2019; AIMCo’s exact split has not been publicly disclosed.",
